If you are parsing user-defined strings like player names, you may want to convert special characters to their [XML entities](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Character_encodings_in_HTML#XML_character_references) as a precaution beforehand, otherwise the result might be corrupted.

```sqf
private _escapeXML =
{
    _this
    regexReplace ["&", "&amp;"]
    regexReplace ["<", "&lt;"]
    regexReplace [">", "&gt;"]
    regexReplace ['"', "&quot;"]
    regexReplace ["'", "&apos;"]
};

private _name = '<A&M> Paul "Bear" Bryant';
private _escapedName = _name call _escapeXML;
private _redName = parseText format ["<t color='#ff0000'>%1</t>", _escapedName];
```

